/* Worked solutions for Mathematics — keyed by the exact question text. */
window.SOLUTIONS = window.SOLUTIONS || {};
window.SOLUTIONS['Mathematics'] = {
  'Simplify: 2x + 5x - 3.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Combine the like terms: 2x + 5x = 7x, while the constant -3 has no partner, so the expression simplifies to 7x - 3.' },
  'What is 15% of 200?': { t: 'Financial arithmetic', e: '15% of 200 = 15/100 x 200 = 30.' },
  'In a class of 40 students, 25 offer Physics, 18 offer Chemistry and 5 offer neither. How many offer both subjects?': { t: 'Sets and Venn diagrams', e: 'Students taking at least one subject = 40 - 5 = 35, so 25 + 18 - both = 35, which gives both = 8.' },
  'Convert 1011 base 2 to base 10.': { t: 'Number bases', e: 'Expand by powers of 2: 1x2^3 + 0x2^2 + 1x2^1 + 1x2^0 = 8 + 0 + 2 + 1 = 11.' },
  'Convert 45 base 10 to base 2.': { t: 'Number bases', e: 'Write 45 as 32 + 8 + 4 + 1, which selects the bits 101101, and indeed 101101 base 2 = 45.' },
  'Simplify: sqrt(50).': { t: 'Number operations', e: 'sqrt(50) = sqrt(25 x 2) = sqrt(25) x sqrt(2) = 5sqrt(2).' },
  'Evaluate: log base 2 of 32.': { t: 'Indices and logarithms', e: 'Since 2^5 = 32, log base 2 of 32 = 5.' },
  'Simplify: 2^3 x 2^4.': { t: 'Indices and logarithms', e: 'When multiplying powers of the same base you add the indices: 2^3 x 2^4 = 2^7 = 128.' },
  'Divide N60 in the ratio 2 : 3. What is the larger share?': { t: 'Number operations', e: 'There are 2 + 3 = 5 parts, each worth 60/5 = N12, so the larger share is 3 x 12 = N36.' },
  'Factorise: x^2 - 9.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'It is a difference of two squares, a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b), so x^2 - 9 = (x - 3)(x + 3).' },
  'Solve the equation: 3x - 7 = 14.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Add 7 to both sides to get 3x = 21, then divide by 3 to get x = 7.' },
  'Solve the simultaneous equations x + y = 10 and x - y = 4.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Adding the equations gives 2x = 14, so x = 7, and substituting back gives y = 10 - 7 = 3.' },
  'The angles of a triangle are in the ratio 2 : 3 : 4. Find the largest angle.': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'The parts total 2 + 3 + 4 = 9 and 180/9 = 20 degrees per part, so the largest angle is 4 x 20 = 80 degrees.' },
  'Find the area of a circle of radius 7 cm. Take pi = 22/7.': { t: 'Mensuration', e: 'Area = pi r^2 = 22/7 x 7 x 7 = 22 x 7 = 154 cm^2.' },
  'Find the perimeter of a rectangle of length 12 cm and breadth 5 cm.': { t: 'Mensuration', e: 'Perimeter = 2(length + breadth) = 2(12 + 5) = 2 x 17 = 34 cm.' },
  'Find the volume of a cube of side 5 cm.': { t: 'Mensuration', e: 'Volume of a cube = side^3 = 5 x 5 x 5 = 125 cm^3.' },
  'Evaluate: sin 30 degrees.': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'From the standard angle values, sin 30 degrees = 1/2.' },
  'The value of tan 45 degrees is:': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'In a 45-45-90 triangle the opposite and adjacent sides are equal, so tan 45 degrees = 1/1 = 1.' },
  'Find the mean of 2, 4, 6, 8 and 10.': { t: 'Statistics', e: 'Mean = (2 + 4 + 6 + 8 + 10)/5 = 30/5 = 6.' },
  'Find the median of 3, 5, 7, 9 and 11.': { t: 'Statistics', e: 'The five values are already ordered, and the middle one is 7, so the median is 7.' },
  'Find the mode of 2, 3, 3, 4, 5, 3 and 4.': { t: 'Statistics', e: 'The value 3 occurs three times, more than any other value, so the mode is 3.' },
  'Find the range of 10, 15, 20 and 25.': { t: 'Statistics', e: 'Range = largest value - smallest value = 25 - 10 = 15.' },
  'A fair die is thrown once. What is the probability of getting a 6?': { t: 'Probability', e: 'A die has 6 equally likely faces and only one of them shows a 6, so the probability is 1/6.' },
  'Find the simple interest on N5,000 at 10% per annum for 2 years.': { t: 'Financial arithmetic', e: 'Simple interest = P x R x T/100 = 5000 x 10 x 2/100 = N1,000.' },
  'Find the amount after 2 years if N1,000 is invested at 10% per annum compound interest.': { t: 'Financial arithmetic', e: 'Amount = 1000 x (1 + 10/100)^2 = 1000 x 1.21 = N1,210.' },
  'Find the 10th term of the sequence 2, 5, 8, 11, ...': { t: 'Sequences and series', e: 'The common difference is 3, so the 10th term = a + 9d = 2 + 9 x 3 = 29.' },
  'Find the sum of the first 10 terms of the arithmetic progression 3, 7, 11, ...': { t: 'Sequences and series', e: 'Here a = 3 and d = 4, so the 10th term = 3 + 9 x 4 = 39 and S10 = 10/2 x (3 + 39) = 5 x 42 = 210.' },
  'If a = (3, 4) and b = (1, 2), find a + b.': { t: 'Vectors and matrices', e: 'Add corresponding components: (3 + 1, 4 + 2) = (4, 6).' },
  'Find the determinant of the 2 x 2 matrix with first row 3, 1 and second row 2, 4.': { t: 'Vectors and matrices', e: 'Determinant = (3 x 4) - (1 x 2) = 12 - 2 = 10.' },
  'Evaluate: 5P2.': { t: 'Permutations and combinations', e: '5P2 = 5!/(5 - 2)! = 5 x 4 = 20.' },
  'Evaluate: 6C2.': { t: 'Permutations and combinations', e: '6C2 = 6!/(2! x 4!) = (6 x 5)/2 = 15.' },
  'The actual value of a quantity is 20 and its measured value is 21. Find the percentage error.': { t: 'Financial arithmetic', e: 'The error is 21 - 20 = 1, so percentage error = (1/20) x 100% = 5%.' },
  'Simplify: x^5 / x^2.': { t: 'Indices and logarithms', e: 'Dividing powers of the same base subtracts the indices: 5 - 2 = 3, so the result is x^3.' },
  'Make x the subject of the formula v = u + ax.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Subtract u from both sides to get v - u = ax, then divide by a to obtain x = (v - u)/a.' },
  'The roots of the equation x^2 - 5x + 6 = 0 are:': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Factorise: x^2 - 5x + 6 = (x - 2)(x - 3) = 0, so the roots are 2 and 3.' },
  'Find the gradient of the line joining (1, 2) and (3, 6).': { t: 'Coordinate geometry', e: 'Gradient = (change in y)/(change in x) = (6 - 2)/(3 - 1) = 4/2 = 2.' },
  'The angle subtended by an arc at the circumference of a circle is 65 degrees. Find the angle subtended by the same arc at the centre.': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'The angle at the centre is twice the angle at the circumference, so it is 2 x 65 = 130 degrees.' },
  'Find the total surface area of a sphere of radius 7 cm. Take pi = 22/7.': { t: 'Mensuration', e: 'Surface area = 4 pi r^2 = 4 x 22/7 x 7 x 7 = 4 x 154 = 616 cm^2.' },
  'Two triangles are similar and the ratio of their corresponding sides is 2 : 3. If the area of the smaller triangle is 16 cm^2, find the area of the larger triangle.': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'Areas of similar triangles are in the square of the side ratio, so 16 : A = 4 : 9, giving A = 16 x 9/4 = 36 cm^2.' },
  'Simplify: sin^2 theta + cos^2 theta.': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'By the Pythagorean identity, sin^2 theta + cos^2 theta = 1 for every angle theta.' },
  'Express 0.00045 in standard form.': { t: 'Number operations', e: 'Move the decimal point 4 places to the right to get 4.5, so 0.00045 = 4.5 x 10^-4.' },
  'Find the HCF of 12, 18 and 24.': { t: 'Number operations', e: '12 = 2^2 x 3, 18 = 2 x 3^2 and 24 = 2^3 x 3, so the highest common factor is 2^2 x 3 = 6.' },
  'Find the LCM of 4, 6 and 8.': { t: 'Number operations', e: '4 = 2^2, 6 = 2 x 3 and 8 = 2^3, so the LCM takes the highest powers: 2^3 x 3 = 24.' },
  'Rationalise the denominator: 1/(sqrt(3) - 1).': { t: 'Number operations', e: 'Multiply top and bottom by the conjugate sqrt(3) + 1: (sqrt(3) + 1)/(3 - 1) = (sqrt(3) + 1)/2.' },
  'Simplify: 3(2x - 4) + 2(x + 5).': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Expand to get 6x - 12 + 2x + 10, then collect like terms: 8x - 2.' },
  'Solve the equation: 2(x + 3) = 4x - 2.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Expand to 2x + 6 = 4x - 2, then rearrange to 8 = 2x, so x = 4.' },
  'How many solutions do the simultaneous equations 3x + 2y = 12 and 6x + 4y = 24 have?': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'The second equation is exactly twice the first, so both equations describe the same line and there are infinitely many solutions.' },
  'If log base 10 of x = 2, find x.': { t: 'Indices and logarithms', e: 'log base 10 of x = 2 means x = 10^2 = 100.' },
  'Simplify: (2/3)^3.': { t: 'Indices and logarithms', e: 'Raise numerator and denominator to the power 3: 2^3/3^3 = 8/27.' },
  'Evaluate: 27^(2/3).': { t: 'Indices and logarithms', e: '27^(2/3) = (cube root of 27)^2 = 3^2 = 9.' },
  'Simplify: sqrt(72).': { t: 'Number operations', e: 'sqrt(72) = sqrt(36 x 2) = sqrt(36) x sqrt(2) = 6sqrt(2).' },
  'Expand and simplify: (x + 4)(x - 6).': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Multiplying out gives x^2 - 6x + 4x - 24, and collecting the middle terms gives x^2 - 2x - 24.' },
  'Factorise: 2x^2 + 7x + 3.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Split the middle term using factors of 2 x 3 = 6 that add to 7: 2x^2 + 6x + x + 3 = 2x(x + 3) + 1(x + 3) = (2x + 1)(x + 3).' },
  'Find the quadratic equation whose roots are 2 and -5.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Sum of roots = 2 + (-5) = -3 and product = -10, so x^2 - (sum)x + product = x^2 + 3x - 10 = 0.' },
  'y varies directly as x and y = 12 when x = 3. Find y when x = 5.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'y = kx gives 12 = 3k so k = 4, and when x = 5, y = 4 x 5 = 20.' },
  'y varies inversely as x and y = 6 when x = 2. Find y when x = 3.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'y = k/x gives k = xy = 12, so when x = 3, y = 12/3 = 4.' },
  'A car travels 180 km in 3 hours. Find its average speed.': { t: 'Number operations', e: 'Speed = distance/time = 180/3 = 60 km/h.' },
  'Find the distance between the points (0, 0) and (3, 4).': { t: 'Coordinate geometry', e: 'Distance = sqrt((3 - 0)^2 + (4 - 0)^2) = sqrt(9 + 16) = sqrt(25) = 5.' },
  'Find the equation of a line with gradient 3 passing through the point (0, -2).': { t: 'Coordinate geometry', e: 'Using y = mx + c with m = 3 and y-intercept c = -2 gives y = 3x - 2.' },
  'Each interior angle of a regular polygon is 140 degrees. Find the number of sides.': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'The exterior angle is 180 - 140 = 40 degrees, and the exterior angles total 360 degrees, so n = 360/40 = 9.' },
  'Each exterior angle of a regular polygon is 40 degrees. Find the number of sides.': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'Exterior angles of any polygon sum to 360 degrees, so n = 360/40 = 9.' },
  'Find the sum of the interior angles of a hexagon.': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'Sum = (n - 2) x 180 = (6 - 2) x 180 = 720 degrees.' },
  'Find the circumference of a circle of radius 14 cm. Take pi = 22/7.': { t: 'Mensuration', e: 'Circumference = 2 pi r = 2 x 22/7 x 14 = 2 x 44 = 88 cm.' },
  'Find the area of a triangle with base 10 cm and height 6 cm.': { t: 'Mensuration', e: 'Area = 1/2 x base x height = 1/2 x 10 x 6 = 30 cm^2.' },
  'Find the area of a parallelogram with base 12 cm and height 5 cm.': { t: 'Mensuration', e: 'Area = base x perpendicular height = 12 x 5 = 60 cm^2.' },
  'Find the area of a sector of a circle of radius 14 cm and angle 90 degrees. Take pi = 22/7.': { t: 'Mensuration', e: 'Area = (90/360) x pi r^2 = 1/4 x 22/7 x 196 = 1/4 x 616 = 154 cm^2.' },
  'Find the volume of a cone of radius 7 cm and height 15 cm. Take pi = 22/7.': { t: 'Mensuration', e: 'Volume = 1/3 pi r^2 h = 1/3 x 22/7 x 49 x 15 = 22 x 7 x 5 = 770 cm^3.' },
  'Find the volume of a cuboid of dimensions 8 m by 5 m by 4 m.': { t: 'Mensuration', e: 'Volume = length x breadth x height = 8 x 5 x 4 = 160 m^3.' },
  'Find the length of the hypotenuse of a right-angled triangle with legs 6 cm and 8 cm.': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'By Pythagoras, c = sqrt(6^2 + 8^2) = sqrt(36 + 64) = sqrt(100) = 10 cm.' },
  'In a right-angled triangle, sin theta = 3/5. Find cos theta.': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'sin theta = opposite/hypotenuse = 3/5, so the adjacent side = sqrt(25 - 9) = 4 and cos theta = adjacent/hypotenuse = 4/5.' },
  'Evaluate: 2 sin 30 degrees + 3 cos 0 degrees.': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'sin 30 degrees = 1/2 and cos 0 degrees = 1, so 2 x 1/2 + 3 x 1 = 1 + 3 = 4.' },
  'The angle of elevation of the top of a tower from a point 30 m away is 30 degrees. Find the height of the tower.': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'tan 30 degrees = height/30, so height = 30 tan 30 degrees = 30/sqrt(3) = 10sqrt(3) m.' },
  'Find the mean of the first 5 positive integers.': { t: 'Statistics', e: 'Mean = (1 + 2 + 3 + 4 + 5)/5 = 15/5 = 3.' },
  'The marks of five students are 4, 6, 8, 10 and 12. Find the median.': { t: 'Statistics', e: 'The marks are already in order, and the middle value of the five is 8.' },
  'A bag contains 3 red balls and 5 blue balls. Find the probability of picking a red ball.': { t: 'Probability', e: 'There are 3 red balls out of 3 + 5 = 8 balls in total, so the probability is 3/8.' },
  'Two fair coins are tossed. What is the probability of getting two heads?': { t: 'Probability', e: 'There are 4 equally likely outcomes (HH, HT, TH, TT) and only HH is favourable, so the probability is 1/4.' },
  'In how many ways can the letters of the word MATH be arranged?': { t: 'Permutations and combinations', e: 'All 4 letters are different, so the number of arrangements is 4! = 4 x 3 x 2 x 1 = 24.' },
  'In how many ways can 3 persons be selected from a group of 5?': { t: 'Permutations and combinations', e: 'Selection does not depend on order, so 5C3 = 5!/(3! x 2!) = (5 x 4)/2 = 10.' },
  'Evaluate: 4!.': { t: 'Permutations and combinations', e: '4! = 4 x 3 x 2 x 1 = 24.' },
  'Find the 15th term of an arithmetic progression with first term 3 and common difference 4.': { t: 'Sequences and series', e: 'a15 = a + 14d = 3 + 14 x 4 = 3 + 56 = 59.' },
  'Find the sum to infinity of the geometric progression 8, 4, 2, 1, ...': { t: 'Sequences and series', e: 'With a = 8 and r = 1/2, S(infinity) = a/(1 - r) = 8/(1 - 1/2) = 8/(1/2) = 16.' },
  'Find the 6th term of the geometric progression 2, 6, 18, ...': { t: 'Sequences and series', e: 'The common ratio is 3, so t6 = a r^5 = 2 x 3^5 = 2 x 243 = 486.' },
  'Find the simple interest on N8,000 at 5% per annum for 3 years.': { t: 'Financial arithmetic', e: 'I = P x R x T/100 = 8000 x 5 x 3/100 = N1,200.' },
  'Find the amount on N5,000 after 2 years at 4% per annum simple interest.': { t: 'Financial arithmetic', e: 'Interest = 5000 x 4 x 2/100 = N400, so the amount = 5,000 + 400 = N5,400.' },
  'Find the amount on N2,000 after 2 years at 5% per annum compound interest.': { t: 'Financial arithmetic', e: 'Amount = 2000 x (1.05)^2 = 2000 x 1.1025 = N2,205.' },
  'In a survey of 200 students, 120 like football and 90 like basketball. If every student likes at least one of the games, how many like both?': { t: 'Sets and Venn diagrams', e: '120 + 90 - both = 200, so both = 210 - 200 = 10.' },
  'In a class, 18 students take History, 12 take Geography and 5 take both. How many take at least one of the two subjects?': { t: 'Sets and Venn diagrams', e: 'n(History or Geography) = 18 + 12 - 5 = 25.' },
  'Convert 10110 base 2 to base 10.': { t: 'Number bases', e: '1x2^4 + 0x2^3 + 1x2^2 + 1x2^1 + 0x2^0 = 16 + 0 + 4 + 2 + 0 = 22.' },
  'Convert 54 base 10 to base 4.': { t: 'Number bases', e: 'Divide 54 by 4 repeatedly: 54 = 13 remainder 2, 13 = 3 remainder 1, 3 = 0 remainder 3, so reading the remainders upwards gives 312 base 4.' },
  'Simplify: 1/2 + 1/3.': { t: 'Number operations', e: 'Using the common denominator 6: 3/6 + 2/6 = 5/6.' },
  'Find the value of x if 2^x = 32.': { t: 'Indices and logarithms', e: 'Since 32 = 2^5, the equation 2^x = 2^5 gives x = 5.' },
  'Simplify: log 100 + log 10.': { t: 'Indices and logarithms', e: 'log 100 = 2 and log 10 = 1, so the sum is 2 + 1 = 3.' },
  'Given that log 2 = 0.3010, find log 8.': { t: 'Indices and logarithms', e: 'log 8 = log 2^3 = 3 log 2 = 3 x 0.3010 = 0.9030.' },
  'Given that log 5 = 0.6990, find log 50.': { t: 'Indices and logarithms', e: 'log 50 = log(5 x 10) = log 5 + log 10 = 0.6990 + 1 = 1.6990.' },
  'Simplify: (2x^2 y)(3x y^3).': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Multiply the coefficients and add the indices of matching bases: 2 x 3 = 6, x^2 x x = x^3 and y x y^3 = y^4, giving 6x^3y^4.' },
  'If log base x of 81 = 4, find x.': { t: 'Indices and logarithms', e: 'log base x of 81 = 4 means x^4 = 81, and since 3^4 = 81 we have x = 3.' },
  'Evaluate: 1/(2^-3).': { t: 'Indices and logarithms', e: 'A negative index inverts the power: 1/(2^-3) = 2^3 = 8.' },
  'Evaluate: (1/2)^-2.': { t: 'Indices and logarithms', e: 'The negative index flips the fraction: (1/2)^-2 = 2^2 = 4.' },
  'Express 32 as a power of 2.': { t: 'Indices and logarithms', e: '32 = 2 x 2 x 2 x 2 x 2, that is five 2s multiplied together, so 32 = 2^5.' },
  'Simplify: sqrt(18) + sqrt(8).': { t: 'Number operations', e: 'sqrt(18) = 3sqrt(2) and sqrt(8) = 2sqrt(2), so adding gives 5sqrt(2).' },
  'Rationalise the denominator: 2/sqrt(5).': { t: 'Number operations', e: 'Multiply top and bottom by sqrt(5): 2 x sqrt(5)/(sqrt(5) x sqrt(5)) = 2sqrt(5)/5.' },
  'Expand and simplify: (x - 3)^2.': { t: 'Algebra', e: '(x - 3)^2 = x^2 - 2 x 3 x x + 3^2 = x^2 - 6x + 9.' },
  'Factorise: x^2 + 6x + 9.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'It is a perfect square trinomial since 3 + 3 = 6 and 3 x 3 = 9, so x^2 + 6x + 9 = (x + 3)^2.' },
  'Factorise completely: 3x^2 - 12.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'First take out the common factor 3 to get 3(x^2 - 4), then use the difference of squares: 3(x - 2)(x + 2).' },
  'Solve the equation: x^2 = 49. Find all the possible values of x.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Taking square roots of both sides gives x = 7 or x = -7, because (-7)^2 is also 49.' },
  'Solve the equation: 5x + 2 = 3x + 10.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Subtract 3x and 2 from both sides: 2x = 8, so x = 4.' },
  'Solve the simultaneous equations x + y = 11 and 2x - y = 10. Find x.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Adding the two equations eliminates y and gives 3x = 21, so x = 7 (and y = 4).' },
  'A rectangle has area 48 cm^2 and length 8 cm. Find its perimeter.': { t: 'Mensuration', e: 'Breadth = area/length = 48/8 = 6 cm, so perimeter = 2(8 + 6) = 28 cm.' },
  'The circumference of a circle is 44 cm. Take pi = 22/7. Find the radius.': { t: 'Mensuration', e: 'From 44 = 2 x 22/7 x r we get r = 44 x 7/44 = 7 cm.' },
  'Find the length of an arc of a sector of radius 10 cm and angle 90 degrees. Take pi = 3.14.': { t: 'Mensuration', e: 'Arc = (90/360) x 2 x 3.14 x 10 = 1/4 x 62.8 = 15.7 cm.' },
  'Find the volume of a sphere of radius 3 cm. Take pi = 3.14.': { t: 'Mensuration', e: 'Volume = 4/3 pi r^3 = 4/3 x 3.14 x 27 = 4 x 3.14 x 9 = 113.04 cm^3.' },
  'Find the curved surface area of a cylinder of radius 7 cm and height 10 cm. Take pi = 22/7.': { t: 'Mensuration', e: 'Curved area = 2 pi r h = 2 x 22/7 x 7 x 10 = 440 cm^2.' },
  'If sin theta = 0.5 and theta is acute, find theta.': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: '0.5 is the same as 1/2, and sin 30 degrees = 1/2, so the acute angle theta = 30 degrees.' },
  'The value of cos 60 degrees is:': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'From the standard angle values, cos 60 degrees = 1/2.' },
  'The value of tan 60 degrees is:': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'tan 60 degrees = sin 60 degrees/cos 60 degrees = (sqrt(3)/2)/(1/2) = sqrt(3).' },
  'The angle of elevation of a tower from a point P is 45 degrees and P is 50 m from the base of the tower. Find the height of the tower.': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'tan 45 degrees = height/50 and tan 45 degrees = 1, so height = 50 x 1 = 50 m.' },
  'The bearing of B from A is 070 degrees. Find the bearing of A from B.': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'The back bearing is found by adding 180 degrees: 70 + 180 = 250 degrees.' },
  'Find the mean of 4, 8, 10 and 12.': { t: 'Statistics', e: 'Mean = (4 + 8 + 10 + 12)/4 = 34/4 = 8.5.' },
  'Find the mode of 5, 7, 7, 9, 11, 7 and 3.': { t: 'Statistics', e: 'The value 7 occurs three times, more than any other value, so the mode is 7.' },
  'Find the range of 12, 4, 18, 7 and 20.': { t: 'Statistics', e: 'Range = largest value - smallest value = 20 - 4 = 16.' },
  'A fair die is thrown once. What is the probability of getting a prime number?': { t: 'Probability', e: 'The prime numbers on a die are 2, 3 and 5, so 3 favourable outcomes out of 6 give 3/6 = 1/2.' },
  'A card is drawn from a standard pack of 52 cards. What is the probability that it is a king?': { t: 'Probability', e: 'There are 4 kings among the 52 cards, so the probability is 4/52 = 1/13.' },
  'The probability that an event occurs is 0.3. What is the probability that it does not occur?': { t: 'Probability', e: 'An event and its complement sum to 1, so the probability it does not occur is 1 - 0.3 = 0.7.' },
  'Evaluate: 5P3.': { t: 'Permutations and combinations', e: '5P3 = 5!/(5 - 3)! = 5 x 4 x 3 = 60.' },
  'Evaluate: 6C4.': { t: 'Permutations and combinations', e: '6C4 = 6C2 = (6 x 5)/2 = 15.' },
  'In how many ways can 5 different books be arranged on a shelf?': { t: 'Permutations and combinations', e: 'The number of arrangements of 5 distinct books is 5! = 5 x 4 x 3 x 2 x 1 = 120.' },
  'In how many ways can 2 captains be chosen from 8 players?': { t: 'Permutations and combinations', e: 'Order does not matter for a selection, so 8C2 = (8 x 7)/2 = 28.' },
  'Find the sum of the first 10 terms of an arithmetic progression whose first term is 6 and common difference is 3.': { t: 'Sequences and series', e: 'The 10th term = 6 + 9 x 3 = 33, so S10 = 10/2 x (6 + 33) = 5 x 39 = 195.' },
  'A geometric progression has first term 5 and common ratio 2. Find the 4th term.': { t: 'Sequences and series', e: 't4 = a r^3 = 5 x 2^3 = 5 x 8 = 40.' },
  'Find the sum of the first 5 terms of the geometric progression 1, 2, 4, 8, ...': { t: 'Sequences and series', e: 'The five terms are 1, 2, 4, 8 and 16, and 1 + 2 + 4 + 8 + 16 = 31.' },
  'A sum of money doubles in 8 years at simple interest. Find the rate percent per annum.': { t: 'Financial arithmetic', e: 'Doubling means the interest equals the principal, so P = P x R x 8/100, giving R = 100/8 = 12.5%.' },
  'Find the compound interest on N10,000 at 5% per annum for 2 years.': { t: 'Financial arithmetic', e: 'Amount = 10000 x 1.05^2 = 10000 x 1.1025 = N11,025, so the compound interest = 11,025 - 10,000 = N1,025.' },
  'A trader allows a discount of 10% on an article marked N500. Find the selling price.': { t: 'Financial arithmetic', e: 'Discount = 10/100 x 500 = N50, so the selling price = 500 - 50 = N450.' },
  'An article is bought for N800 and sold for N1,000. Find the percentage profit.': { t: 'Financial arithmetic', e: 'Profit = 1,000 - 800 = 200, and percentage profit = (200/800) x 100% = 25%.' },
  'A number is increased by 20% and the result is 90. Find the number.': { t: 'Financial arithmetic', e: '120% of the number equals 90, so the number = 90 x 100/120 = 75.' },
  'Solve the equation: |2x - 6| = 4.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Either 2x - 6 = 4, which gives x = 5, or 2x - 6 = -4, which gives x = 1, so x = 1 or x = 5.' },
  'Simplify: 1/2 - 1/3 + 1/6.': { t: 'Number operations', e: 'Using the common denominator 6: 3/6 - 2/6 + 1/6 = 2/6 = 1/3.' },
  'Express 0.125 as a fraction in its lowest terms.': { t: 'Number operations', e: '0.125 = 125/1000, and dividing numerator and denominator by 125 gives 1/8.' },
  'Express 0.75 as a percentage.': { t: 'Financial arithmetic', e: 'Multiply by 100: 0.75 x 100% = 75%.' },
  'Increase 200 by 15%.': { t: 'Financial arithmetic', e: '15% of 200 = 30, so 200 + 30 = 230.' },
  'Decrease 250 by 20%.': { t: 'Financial arithmetic', e: '20% of 250 = 50, so 250 - 50 = 200.' },
  'What is 40% of 50?': { t: 'Financial arithmetic', e: '40% of 50 = 40/100 x 50 = 20.' },
  'Simplify: 3/4 divided by 1/2.': { t: 'Number operations', e: 'Dividing by a fraction means multiplying by its reciprocal: 3/4 x 2/1 = 6/4 = 3/2.' },
  'Find the HCF of 24, 36 and 60.': { t: 'Number operations', e: '24 = 2^3 x 3, 36 = 2^2 x 3^2 and 60 = 2^2 x 3 x 5, so the highest common factor is 2^2 x 3 = 12.' },
  'Find the LCM of 9, 12 and 15.': { t: 'Number operations', e: '9 = 3^2, 12 = 2^2 x 3 and 15 = 3 x 5, so the LCM = 2^2 x 3^2 x 5 = 180.' },
  'Express 35% as a decimal.': { t: 'Financial arithmetic', e: 'Divide by 100: 35% = 35/100 = 0.35.' },
  'Simplify the ratio 150 cm : 2 m.': { t: 'Number operations', e: 'Convert to the same unit first: 150 cm : 200 cm = 150 : 200, and dividing both by 50 gives 3 : 4.' },
  'Two numbers are in the ratio 3 : 5 and their sum is 64. Find the smaller number.': { t: 'Number operations', e: 'There are 3 + 5 = 8 parts totalling 64, so one part = 64/8 = 8 and the smaller number is 3 x 8 = 24.' },
  'On a map the scale is 1 : 50,000. Two towns are 8 cm apart on the map. Find the actual distance between them in km.': { t: 'Number operations', e: 'Actual distance = 8 x 50,000 = 400,000 cm = 4 km.' },
  '5 workers can do a job in 12 days. How many days will 6 workers take to do the same job?': { t: 'Number operations', e: 'The job needs 5 x 12 = 60 worker-days, so 6 workers take 60/6 = 10 days.' },
  'Find the gradient of the line 2x + 3y = 6.': { t: 'Coordinate geometry', e: 'Rearrange into y = mx + c: 3y = -2x + 6, so y = -2/3 x + 2 and the gradient is -2/3.' },
  'Find the x-intercept of the line y = 2x - 8.': { t: 'Coordinate geometry', e: 'At the x-intercept y = 0, so 0 = 2x - 8 gives x = 4.' },
  'Find the distance between the points (-1, -2) and (3, 6).': { t: 'Coordinate geometry', e: 'Distance = sqrt((3 - (-1))^2 + (6 - (-2))^2) = sqrt(4^2 + 8^2) = sqrt(80) = 4sqrt(5).' },
  'Find the midpoint of the line segment joining (2, 6) and (4, 10).': { t: 'Coordinate geometry', e: 'Midpoint = ((2 + 4)/2, (6 + 10)/2) = (3, 8).' },
  'If the matrix A has first row 2, 1 and second row 3, 4, find the matrix 2A.': { t: 'Vectors and matrices', e: 'Multiplying by the scalar 2 doubles every entry, giving first row 4, 2 and second row 6, 8.' },
  'Find the determinant of the 2 x 2 matrix with first row 2, 3 and second row 4, 5.': { t: 'Vectors and matrices', e: 'Determinant = (2 x 5) - (3 x 4) = 10 - 12 = -2.' },
  'If a = (2, -1) and b = (-1, 3), find a - b.': { t: 'Vectors and matrices', e: 'Subtract components: (2 - (-1), -1 - 3) = (3, -4).' },
  'Find the dot product of the vectors (2, 3) and (4, 1).': { t: 'Vectors and matrices', e: 'Dot product = 2 x 4 + 3 x 1 = 8 + 3 = 11.' },
  'Find the unit vector in the direction of (3, 4).': { t: 'Vectors and matrices', e: 'The magnitude is sqrt(3^2 + 4^2) = 5, so dividing each component by 5 gives the unit vector (3/5, 4/5).' },
  'Two angles stand on a straight line. If one is 65 degrees, find the other.': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'Angles on a straight line sum to 180 degrees, so the other angle = 180 - 65 = 115 degrees.' },
  'Three angles of a quadrilateral are 60, 90 and 110 degrees. Find the fourth angle.': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'Angles of a quadrilateral total 360 degrees, so the fourth angle = 360 - (60 + 90 + 110) = 100 degrees.' },
  'An angle inscribed in a semicircle measures:': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'The arc of a semicircle is a 180 degree arc, and the angle at the circumference is half the angle at the centre, so it measures 90 degrees.' },
  'The angle between a tangent to a circle and the radius drawn to the point of contact is:': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'A tangent is perpendicular to the radius at the point of contact, so the angle is 90 degrees.' },
  'Find the area of a trapezium with parallel sides 8 cm and 12 cm and height 5 cm.': { t: 'Mensuration', e: 'Area = 1/2 x (sum of parallel sides) x height = 1/2 x (8 + 12) x 5 = 50 cm^2.' },
  'A wheel of diameter 70 cm rolls over a distance of 1.1 km. How many revolutions does it make? Take pi = 22/7.': { t: 'Mensuration', e: 'Circumference = 22/7 x 70 = 220 cm and 1.1 km = 110,000 cm, so revolutions = 110,000/220 = 500, which is option A.' },
  'A ladder 13 m long rests with its foot 5 m from a vertical wall. How high up the wall does the ladder reach?': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'By Pythagoras the height = sqrt(13^2 - 5^2) = sqrt(169 - 25) = sqrt(144) = 12 m.' },
  'In triangle PQR, angle P = 50 degrees and angle Q = 60 degrees. Find angle R.': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'Angles of a triangle sum to 180 degrees, so R = 180 - 50 - 60 = 70 degrees.' },
  'Find the diagonal of a rectangle of length 12 cm and breadth 5 cm.': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'By Pythagoras the diagonal = sqrt(12^2 + 5^2) = sqrt(144 + 25) = sqrt(169) = 13 cm.' },
  'If sin x = 4/5 and x is acute, find tan x.': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'sin x = opposite/hypotenuse = 4/5 gives opposite = 4 and hypotenuse = 5, so adjacent = sqrt(25 - 16) = 3 and tan x = 4/3.' },
  'In a right-angled triangle the side adjacent to an angle is 8 cm and the hypotenuse is 10 cm. Find the cosine of the angle.': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'cos = adjacent/hypotenuse = 8/10 = 4/5.' },
  'The sum of two numbers is 25 and their difference is 5. Find the larger number.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Adding the sum and the difference gives 2 x larger = 30, so the larger number is 15 (the smaller is 10).' },
  'Find the value of x if 3^(2x) = 81.': { t: 'Indices and logarithms', e: '81 = 3^4, so 3^(2x) = 3^4 gives 2x = 4 and x = 2.' },
  'Simplify: (x^3 y^2)^2.': { t: 'Indices and logarithms', e: 'Multiply each index by the outside index: x^(3 x 2) y^(2 x 2) = x^6 y^4.' },
  'Evaluate: log base 3 of 1.': { t: 'Indices and logarithms', e: 'Since 3^0 = 1, log base 3 of 1 = 0.' },
  'Simplify: log 4 + log 25.': { t: 'Indices and logarithms', e: 'Using the product rule, log 4 + log 25 = log(4 x 25) = log 100 = 2.' },
  'Find the next number in the pattern 2, 4, 8, 16, ...': { t: 'Sequences and series', e: 'Each term is twice the previous one, so the next number is 16 x 2 = 32.' },
  'Find the nth term of the sequence 4, 7, 10, 13, ...': { t: 'Sequences and series', e: 'The common difference is 3 and the first term is 4, so the nth term = 3n + 1 (when n = 1 it gives 4).' },
  'A bag contains 4 red, 5 blue and 6 green balls. Find the probability of picking a ball that is not red.': { t: 'Probability', e: 'The balls that are not red are 5 + 6 = 11 out of 4 + 5 + 6 = 15, so the probability is 11/15.' },
  'How many 3-digit numbers can be formed using the digits 1, 2, 3, 4 and 5 if no digit is repeated?': { t: 'Permutations and combinations', e: 'There are 5 choices for the hundreds digit, 4 for the tens and 3 for the units, giving 5 x 4 x 3 = 60.' },
  'Find the number of permutations of 6 objects taken 2 at a time.': { t: 'Permutations and combinations', e: '6P2 = 6!/(6 - 2)! = 6 x 5 = 30.' },

  /* --- js/questions.js Mathematics entries (unicode text kept exact) --- */
  'Simplify: 2/3 + 3/4': { t: 'Number operations', e: 'The LCM of 3 and 4 is 12: 2/3 = 8/12 and 3/4 = 9/12, so the sum is 8/12 + 9/12 = 17/12.' },
  'If 3x − 5 = 16, what is x?': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Add 5 to both sides: 3x = 21. Divide by 3: x = 7.' },
  'Find the area of a circle of radius 7 cm. (Take π = 22/7)': { t: 'Mensuration', e: 'Area = pi r^2 = 22/7 x 7 x 7 = 154 cm^2.' },
  'What is 15% of ₦200?': { t: 'Financial arithmetic', e: '15% of 200 = 15/100 x 200 = ₦30.' },
  'Solve: 2(x + 3) = 18': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Expand: 2x + 6 = 18, so 2x = 12 and x = 6.' },
  'A right-angled triangle has sides 3 cm, 4 cm and 5 cm. Its area is:': { t: 'Mensuration', e: 'The two shorter sides are the base and the height: area = 1/2 x 3 x 4 = 6 cm^2 (5 cm is the hypotenuse).' },
  'Simplify: √144 + √25': { t: 'Number operations', e: 'sqrt(144) = 12 and sqrt(25) = 5, so the sum is 12 + 5 = 17.' },
  'Simple interest on ₦5,000 at 10% per annum for 2 years is:': { t: 'Financial arithmetic', e: 'I = PRT/100 = 5000 x 10 x 2 / 100 = ₦1,000.' },
  'The mean of 4, 6, 8 and x is 6. Find x.': { t: 'Statistics', e: '(4 + 6 + 8 + x)/4 = 6, so 18 + x = 24 and x = 6.' },
  'If log₁₀ 1000 = x, find x.': { t: 'Indices and logarithms', e: 'log base 10 of 1000 asks: 10 raised to what gives 1000? Since 10^3 = 1000, x = 3.' },
  'The median of 3, 5, 7, 9 and 11 is:': { t: 'Statistics', e: 'The values are already in order and there are five of them, so the middle (third) value, 7, is the median.' },
  'A triangle has base 10 cm and height 5 cm. Its area is:': { t: 'Mensuration', e: 'Area = 1/2 x base x height = 1/2 x 10 x 5 = 25 cm^2.' },
  'Solve the simultaneous equations: x + y = 10 and x − y = 4.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Add the two equations: 2x = 14, so x = 7. Then y = 10 - 7 = 3.' },
  'The probability of getting a head when a fair coin is tossed once is:': { t: 'Probability', e: 'One favourable outcome out of two equally likely outcomes: 1/2.' },
  'The sum of the first 10 natural numbers is:': { t: 'Sequences and series', e: 'n(n + 1)/2 = 10 x 11/2 = 55.' },
  'Factorise: x² − 9': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'This is a difference of two squares: x^2 - 9 = (x - 3)(x + 3).' },
  'The circumference of a circle is 44 cm. Find its radius. (Take π = 22/7)': { t: 'Mensuration', e: 'Circumference = 2 pi r: 44 = 2 x 22/7 x r, so r = 44 x 7 / 44 = 7 cm.' },
  'If 30% of a number is 60, the number is:': { t: 'Financial arithmetic', e: '30% of N = 60 means 0.3N = 60, so the number = 200.' },

  /* --- 2026-10-10: calculus topics --- */
  'Differentiate: y = x^3.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'Power rule: multiply by the index, then reduce it by 1: d/dx(x^3) = 3x^(3 - 1) = 3x^2.' },
  'Find dy/dx if y = 5x^2 - 3x + 7.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'Differentiate term by term: d/dx(5x^2) = 10x, d/dx(-3x) = -3, and the constant 7 differentiates to 0, so dy/dx = 10x - 3.' },
  'Differentiate: y = (2x + 3)^4.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'Chain rule: bring the power down and reduce it, then multiply by the derivative of the bracket: 4(2x + 3)^3 x 2 = 8(2x + 3)^3.' },
  'If y = x^4 - 2x^2, find the second derivative d^2y/dx^2.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'First derivative: dy/dx = 4x^3 - 4x. Differentiate that again: d^2y/dx^2 = 12x^2 - 4.' },
  'Differentiate: y = 3x^2(2x - 1).': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'Expand first: y = 6x^3 - 3x^2, then differentiate: dy/dx = 18x^2 - 6x.' },
  'Differentiate: y = 1/x^2.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'Write it as a power: y = x^(-2). Then dy/dx = -2x^(-3) = -2/x^3.' },
  'Differentiate: y = 2x/(x + 1).': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'Quotient rule: [2(x + 1) - 2x x 1]/(x + 1)^2 = [2x + 2 - 2x]/(x + 1)^2 = 2/(x + 1)^2.' },
  'Differentiate: y = sin x.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'Standard result: the derivative of sin x is cos x.' },
  'Differentiate: y = 2 cos x.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'The derivative of cos x is -sin x, and the constant 2 rides along: dy/dx = -2 sin x.' },
  'Find the derivative of y = x^2 from first principles.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'From first principles: [(x + h)^2 - x^2]/h = [2xh + h^2]/h = 2x + h, and letting h tend to 0 leaves 2x.' },
  'Differentiate: y = x(x^2 - 3).': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'Expand first: y = x^3 - 3x, so dy/dx = 3x^2 - 3.' },
  'If y = 2x^3 - x, find the value of dy/dx at x = -1.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'dy/dx = 6x^2 - 1. At x = -1: 6(1) - 1 = 5.' },
  'Integrate 6x with respect to x.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'The integral of 6x is 6x^2/2 = 3x^2, plus the constant of integration C.' },
  'Integrate (2x + 3) with respect to x.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'Integrate term by term: the integral of 2x is x^2 and the integral of 3 is 3x, so x^2 + 3x + C.' },
  'Integrate x^3 with respect to x.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'Power up and divide by the new power: the integral of x^3 is x^4/4, so x^4/4 + C.' },
  'Evaluate: integral from 0 to 2 of 3x^2 dx.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'The integral of 3x^2 is x^3. Evaluate between the limits: [x^3] from 0 to 2 = 8 - 0 = 8.' },
  'Evaluate: integral from 1 to 3 of (2x + 1) dx.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'The integral of (2x + 1) is x^2 + x. Evaluate: (9 + 3) - (1 + 1) = 12 - 2 = 10.' },
  'Integrate cos x with respect to x.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'Standard result: the integral of cos x is sin x, so sin x + C.' },
  'Evaluate: integral from 0 to 1 of (3x^2 + 2x) dx.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'The integral of (3x^2 + 2x) is x^3 + x^2. Evaluate from 0 to 1: (1 + 1) - 0 = 2.' },
  'Integrate (x^2 - 2x) with respect to x.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'Integrate term by term: x^3/3 - x^2 + C. (Check: differentiating x^3/3 - x^2 gives x^2 - 2x.)' },
  'Evaluate: integral from 1 to 2 of x^3 dx.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'The integral of x^3 is x^4/4. Evaluate from 1 to 2: 16/4 - 1/4 = 15/4.' },
  'Integrate 1/x^2 with respect to x.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'Write 1/x^2 as x^(-2), then the integral is x^(-1)/(-1) = -1/x, so -1/x + C.' },
  'Integrate sin x with respect to x.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'Standard result: the integral of sin x is -cos x, so -cos x + C.' },
  'Find the area under the curve y = x^2 from x = 0 to x = 3.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'Area = the integral of x^2 from 0 to 3 = [x^3/3] from 0 to 3 = 27/3 - 0 = 9 square units.' },
  'The displacement s metres of a particle after t seconds is s = t^3 - 3t^2. Find its velocity when t = 2.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'Velocity is the derivative of displacement: v = 3t^2 - 6t. At t = 2: 3(4) - 6(2) = 12 - 12 = 0 m/s.' },
  'A particle moves such that its displacement s metres after t seconds is s = 2t^3 + t. Find its acceleration when t = 2.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'v = ds/dt = 6t^2 + 1, so a = dv/dt = 12t. At t = 2: a = 24 m/s^2.' },
  'Find the minimum value of y = x^2 - 4x + 7.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'dy/dx = 2x - 4 = 0 gives x = 2. Substituting: y = 4 - 8 + 7 = 3 (a minimum, since d^2y/dx^2 = 2 > 0).' },
  'Find the equation of the tangent to the curve y = x^2 - 4x at the point where x = 3.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'At x = 3: y = 9 - 12 = -3 and the gradient dy/dx = 2x - 4 = 2. Tangent: y - (-3) = 2(x - 3), so y = 2x - 9.' },
  'Find the maximum value of y = 6x - x^2.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'dy/dx = 6 - 2x = 0 gives x = 3. The value there: y = 18 - 9 = 9 (a maximum, since d^2y/dx^2 = -2 < 0).' },
  'The radius of a circle increases at the rate of 0.1 cm/s. Find the rate of increase of its area when the radius is 5 cm.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'A = pi r^2, so dA/dr = 2pi r. Chain rule: dA/dt = 2pi r x dr/dt = 2pi(5)(0.1) = pi cm^2/s.' },
  'Find the x-coordinates of the turning points of the curve y = x^3 - 3x.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'dy/dx = 3x^2 - 3 = 0 gives x^2 = 1, so x = 1 or x = -1.' },
  'Use calculus to estimate the change in y = x^2 when x increases from 4 to 4.01.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'dy/dx = 2x = 8 at x = 4. Change in y is about dy/dx x change in x = 8 x 0.01 = 0.08.' },
  'A body moves with velocity v = 6t^2 m/s. Find the distance covered in the first 2 seconds.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'Distance is the integral of velocity: s = 2t^3. From 0 to 2 seconds: 2(8) - 0 = 16 m.' },
  'The displacement s metres of a particle after t seconds is s = t^2 - 4t + 3. Find the time when the particle is momentarily at rest.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'At rest means ds/dt = 0. v = 2t - 4 = 0, so t = 2 s.' },
  'A rectangle has a perimeter of 20 cm. Find its maximum possible area.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'If the length is x, the breadth is 10 - x, so A = x(10 - x) = 10x - x^2. dA/dx = 10 - 2x = 0 gives x = 5, and A = 5 x 5 = 25 cm^2 (a maximum, since d^2A/dx^2 = -2 < 0).' },
  'Find the gradient of the normal to the curve y = x^2 at the point x = 2.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'The tangent gradient is dy/dx = 2x = 4 at x = 2. The normal is perpendicular, so its gradient is -1/4.' },

  /* --- 2026-10-10: curves, trig graphs, locus, data, transformations --- */
  'Find the radius of the circle x^2 + y^2 = 49.': { t: 'Coordinate geometry', e: 'The circle x^2 + y^2 = r^2 has radius r: here r^2 = 49, so r = 7.' },
  'The centre of the circle (x - 3)^2 + (y + 2)^2 = 25 is:': { t: 'Coordinate geometry', e: 'Compared with (x - a)^2 + (y - b)^2 = r^2, a = 3 and b = -2, so the centre is (3, -2).' },
  'The radius of the circle (x + 1)^2 + (y - 4)^2 = 16 is:': { t: 'Coordinate geometry', e: 'The right side is r^2 = 16, so r = 4.' },
  'Find the equation of the circle with centre (0, 0) and radius 6.': { t: 'Coordinate geometry', e: 'Centre (0, 0) with radius r gives x^2 + y^2 = r^2, so x^2 + y^2 = 6^2 = 36.' },
  'Which of these points lies on the curve y = x^2 - x - 2?': { t: 'Coordinate geometry', e: 'Substitute each point: at (0, -2), y = 0^2 - 0 - 2 = -2, which matches. The others give y-values that do not match their second coordinate.' },
  'The curve y = x^2 - 4x crosses the x-axis at:': { t: 'Coordinate geometry', e: 'On the x-axis y = 0: x^2 - 4x = x(x - 4) = 0, so x = 0 or x = 4.' },
  'Find the points where the line y = 3x - 2 meets the curve y = x^2.': { t: 'Coordinate geometry', e: 'Set x^2 = 3x - 2, so x^2 - 3x + 2 = (x - 1)(x - 2) = 0, giving x = 1 and x = 2. The matching y-values are 1 and 4, so the points are (1, 1) and (2, 4).' },
  'The line of symmetry of the curve y = x^2 - 6x + 5 is:': { t: 'Coordinate geometry', e: 'A parabola y = ax^2 + bx + c has its axis at x = -b/(2a) = 6/2 = 3, so the line of symmetry is x = 3.' },
  'Find the radius of the circle x^2 + y^2 - 8x + 6y + 21 = 0.': { t: 'Coordinate geometry', e: 'Complete the squares: (x - 4)^2 - 16 + (y + 3)^2 - 9 + 21 = 0, which tidies to (x - 4)^2 + (y + 3)^2 = 4, so the radius is 2.' },
  'The period of the graph of y = sin 2x is:': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'For y = sin kx the period is 360/k degrees, so 360/2 = 180 degrees.' },
  'The maximum value of y = 3 sin x is:': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'sin x never rises above 1, so 3 sin x peaks at 3 (at x = 90 degrees).' },
  'The amplitude of y = 5 cos x is:': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'The amplitude is the number multiplying cos x: 5.' },
  'The period of the graph of y = tan x is:': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'The tangent graph repeats every 180 degrees.' },
  'How many solutions does sin x = 1/2 have for 0 degrees <= x <= 360 degrees?': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'sin x = 1/2 at x = 30 degrees and x = 150 degrees - sine is positive in the first and second quadrants - so there are two solutions.' },
  'The range of the function y = 2 + sin x is:': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'sin x runs between -1 and 1, so adding 2 lifts the whole range to between 1 and 3.' },
  'In the range 0 degrees <= x <= 360 degrees, y = cos x has its maximum at:': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'cos x = 1 at x = 0 and x = 360 degrees, so the graph peaks at both ends of the range.' },
  'The graph of y = tan x is undefined at:': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'tan x = sin x / cos x, and cos x = 0 at 90 and 270 degrees, so tan is undefined there (the vertical asymptotes).' },
  'The maximum value of y = sin x + cos x is:': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'The maximum of a sin x + b cos x is sqrt(a^2 + b^2), here sqrt(1 + 1) = sqrt(2), reached at x = 45 degrees.' },
  'The locus of a point equidistant from two fixed points A and B is:': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'Every point on the perpendicular bisector of AB is the same distance from A as from B, so that line is the locus.' },
  'The locus of a point equidistant from two intersecting lines is:': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'Points on the angle bisectors sit equally far from both lines, so the locus is the pair of bisectors.' },
  'The locus of a point at a constant distance r from a fixed point O is:': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'Keeping a fixed distance from a point traces a circle around that point, of radius r.' },
  'The locus of a point at a constant distance d from a fixed straight line is:': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'Every point at distance d from the fixed line lies on one of two parallel lines, one on each side.' },
  'To construct the perpendicular bisector of a segment AB, the compasses must be opened to a radius:': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'A radius greater than half of AB makes the arcs from A and B cross each other; at exactly half they only touch, and below half they never meet.' },
  'The first step in bisecting a given angle is to:': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'An arc drawn from the vertex cuts both arms; the bisector is then built from those two equal-distance points.' },
  'A point P moves so that angle APB = 90 degrees, where A and B are fixed points. The locus of P is:': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'The angle in a semicircle is 90 degrees, so P lies on the circle with AB as diameter.' },
  'To construct a regular hexagon, the compasses are set to the:': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'A regular hexagon has side equal to the radius of its circle, so step around the circle with the compasses set to the radius.' },
  'A circle rolls along a straight line without slipping. The locus of its centre is:': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'The centre stays at the constant height of one radius above the line, tracing a straight line parallel to it.' },
  'On a pie chart, a value of 45 out of a total of 180 is drawn with a sector angle of:': { t: 'Statistics', e: 'Sector angle = 45/180 x 360 = 90 degrees.' },
  'A sector of 60 degrees on a pie chart represents 120 students. The total number of students is:': { t: 'Statistics', e: '60 degrees is 60/360 = 1/6 of the circle, so 120 students are 1/6 of the total: total = 120 x 6 = 720.' },
  'The cumulative frequency curve is also called:': { t: 'Statistics', e: 'The cumulative frequency curve is also known as an ogive.' },
  'Which chart shows class intervals on the x-axis with no gaps between the bars?': { t: 'Statistics', e: 'A histogram has no gaps between bars; the x-axis carries the class intervals and the bar area represents frequency.' },
  'The median of a distribution is read from the cumulative frequency curve at the cumulative frequency equal to:': { t: 'Statistics', e: 'The median sits at cumulative frequency N/2 on the ogive, where N is the total frequency.' },
  'In the distribution 0-9: 4 students, 10-19: 6 students, 20-29: 10 students, the class mark of 20-29 is:': { t: 'Statistics', e: 'Class mark = midpoint of the class = (20 + 29)/2 = 24.5.' },
  'In a bar chart, the height of each bar represents the:': { t: 'Statistics', e: 'Each bar is drawn with height proportional to the frequency of its class.' },
  'The angles of the sectors of a pie chart are 150, 100, 60 and x degrees. Find x.': { t: 'Statistics', e: 'The sectors must total 360: 150 + 100 + 60 + x = 360, so x = 50.' },
  'Given frequencies 2, 5, 3 and 4, the cumulative frequency after the third class is:': { t: 'Statistics', e: 'Add the first three frequencies: 2 + 5 + 3 = 10.' },
  'The image of the point (3, 4) under the translation by vector (-1, 2) is:': { t: 'Vectors and matrices', e: 'Add corresponding components: (3 + (-1), 4 + 2) = (2, 6).' },
  'The reflection of the point (5, -2) in the x-axis is:': { t: 'Vectors and matrices', e: 'Reflection in the x-axis flips the sign of y: (5, -2) becomes (5, 2).' },
  'The reflection of the point (3, 7) in the line y = x is:': { t: 'Vectors and matrices', e: 'Reflection in y = x swaps the coordinates: (3, 7) becomes (7, 3).' },
  'The image of (2, 5) under a rotation of 180 degrees about the origin is:': { t: 'Vectors and matrices', e: 'A half-turn about the origin sends (x, y) to (-x, -y): (2, 5) becomes (-2, -5).' },
  'An enlargement of scale factor 2 maps a triangle of area 6 cm^2 onto a triangle of area:': { t: 'Vectors and matrices', e: 'Area scales by the square of the factor: 6 x 2^2 = 24 cm^2.' },
  'The matrix with first row 1, 0 and second row 0, -1 represents a reflection in the:': { t: 'Vectors and matrices', e: 'The matrix keeps x unchanged and sends y to -y, which is exactly a reflection in the x-axis.' },
  'A translation by the vector (4, -3) moves a point 4 units to the right and:': { t: 'Vectors and matrices', e: 'The second component is -3, so the point moves 3 units down.' },
  'The transformation that turns a shape into its mirror image is a:': { t: 'Vectors and matrices', e: 'Only a reflection reverses a shape into a mirror image; translation, rotation and enlargement never flip it.' },
  'The image of the point (2, 1) under a rotation of 90 degrees anticlockwise about the origin is:': { t: 'Vectors and matrices', e: 'A 90-degree anticlockwise turn about the origin sends (x, y) to (-y, x): (2, 1) becomes (-1, 2).' },

  /* --- 2026-10-11: bank expansion — Number & Numeration --- */
  'Convert 1101 base 2 to base 10.': { t: 'Number bases', e: 'Expand in powers of 2: 1 x 8 + 1 x 4 + 0 x 2 + 1 x 1 = 13.' },
  'Convert 25 base 10 to base 2.': { t: 'Number bases', e: 'Divide 25 by 2 repeatedly and read the remainders from bottom to top: 25 = 11001 base 2.' },
  'Evaluate: 101 base 2 + 11 base 2.': { t: 'Number bases', e: 'In base 10 this is 5 + 3 = 8, and 8 = 1000 base 2.' },
  'Evaluate: 110 base 2 x 11 base 2.': { t: 'Number bases', e: 'Convert first: 110 base 2 = 6 and 11 base 2 = 3. Then 6 x 3 = 18 = 10010 base 2.' },
  'Convert 17 base 8 to base 10.': { t: 'Number bases', e: 'Expand in powers of 8: 1 x 8 + 7 x 1 = 15.' },
  'Evaluate: 1001 base 2 - 110 base 2.': { t: 'Number bases', e: 'In base 10 this is 9 - 6 = 3, and 3 = 11 base 2.' },
  'Simplify: 2/5 + 1/2.': { t: 'Number operations', e: 'Common denominator 10: 4/10 + 5/10 = 9/10.' },
  'Simplify: 3/4 - 2/3.': { t: 'Number operations', e: 'Common denominator 12: 9/12 - 8/12 = 1/12.' },
  'Express 3/8 as a decimal.': { t: 'Number operations', e: 'Divide 3 by 8 to get 0.375.' },
  'Express 0.6 as a fraction in its lowest terms.': { t: 'Number operations', e: '0.6 = 6/10; divide top and bottom by 2 to get 3/5.' },
  'What fraction of 2 hours is 24 minutes?': { t: 'Number operations', e: '2 hours = 120 minutes, so the fraction is 24/120 = 1/5.' },
  'Express 0.333 recurring as a fraction in its lowest terms.': { t: 'Number operations', e: 'Let x = 0.333... Then 10x = 3.333..., so 9x = 3 and x = 1/3.' },
  'A shopkeeper buys an article for N250 and sells it for N300. Find the percentage profit.': { t: 'Financial arithmetic', e: 'Profit = 300 - 250 = N50; percentage profit = 50/250 x 100 = 20%.' },
  'A man earns N40,000 a month. He spends 70% of it and saves the rest. How much does he save?': { t: 'Financial arithmetic', e: 'He saves 30% of his income: 30/100 x 40,000 = N12,000.' },
  'An article marked N2,000 is sold at a discount of 15%. Find the selling price.': { t: 'Financial arithmetic', e: 'Discount = 15/100 x 2,000 = N300, so the selling price is 2,000 - 300 = N1,700.' },
  'The price of a bag rose from N1,500 to N1,800. Find the percentage increase.': { t: 'Financial arithmetic', e: 'Increase = 300; percentage increase = 300/1500 x 100 = 20%.' },
  'Find the simple interest on N12,000 at 8% per annum for 18 months.': { t: 'Financial arithmetic', e: '18 months = 1.5 years, so I = 12,000 x 8 x 1.5 / 100 = N1,440.' },
  'A woman invests N20,000 at 10% per annum compound interest for 2 years. Find the interest earned.': { t: 'Financial arithmetic', e: 'Amount = 20,000 x (1.1)^2 = N24,200, so the interest is 24,200 - 20,000 = N4,200.' },
  'Divide N45 between Ada and Bola in the ratio 4 : 5. How much does Bola get?': { t: 'Number operations', e: 'Total parts = 9, so one part = 45/9 = N5. Bola gets 5 parts = N25.' },
  'A ribbon is cut in the ratio 3 : 5. If the shorter piece is 21 cm, find the total length.': { t: 'Number operations', e: 'One part = 21/3 = 7 cm, so the whole ribbon is 8 parts = 56 cm.' },
  'If 3 oranges cost N45, how much will 7 oranges cost?': { t: 'Number operations', e: 'One orange costs 45/3 = N15, so 7 oranges cost 7 x 15 = N105.' },
  'A car covers 240 km on 20 litres of fuel. How far will it go on 35 litres?': { t: 'Number operations', e: 'Rate = 240/20 = 12 km per litre, so 35 litres gives 35 x 12 = 420 km.' },
  'A map has a scale of 1 : 100,000. Two points are 6 cm apart on the map. Find the real distance between them in km.': { t: 'Number operations', e: '6 cm x 100,000 = 600,000 cm, and 600,000 cm = 6 km.' },
  'It takes 4 machines 9 hours to complete a task. How long will 6 machines take?': { t: 'Number operations', e: 'The task needs 4 x 9 = 36 machine-hours, so 6 machines take 36/6 = 6 hours.' },
  'Simplify: 3^2 x 3^5.': { t: 'Indices and logarithms', e: 'Same base, add the indices: 3^(2 + 5) = 3^7.' },
  'Simplify: 5^8 / 5^6.': { t: 'Indices and logarithms', e: 'Same base, subtract the indices: 5^(8 - 6) = 5^2 = 25.' },
  'Simplify: (4^3)^2.': { t: 'Indices and logarithms', e: 'Power of a power, multiply the indices: 4^(3 x 2) = 4^6.' },
  'Evaluate: 2^-4.': { t: 'Indices and logarithms', e: 'A negative index means reciprocal: 2^-4 = 1/2^4 = 1/16.' },
  'Simplify: 2^n x 8.': { t: 'Indices and logarithms', e: '8 = 2^3, so 2^n x 2^3 = 2^(n + 3).' },
  'Solve: 3^x = 1/27.': { t: 'Indices and logarithms', e: '1/27 = 3^-3, so x = -3.' },
  'Evaluate: log base 5 of 125.': { t: 'Indices and logarithms', e: '125 = 5^3, so the logarithm is 3.' },
  'Evaluate: log base 4 of 1/16.': { t: 'Indices and logarithms', e: '1/16 = 4^-2, so the logarithm is -2.' },
  'Simplify: 2 log 3 + log 4.': { t: 'Indices and logarithms', e: '2 log 3 = log 9, and log 9 + log 4 = log(9 x 4) = log 36.' },
  'Evaluate: log 20 - log 2.': { t: 'Indices and logarithms', e: 'log 20 - log 2 = log(20/2) = log 10 = 1.' },
  'Given that log 2 = 0.3010 and log 3 = 0.4771, find log 6.': { t: 'Indices and logarithms', e: 'log 6 = log 2 + log 3 = 0.3010 + 0.4771 = 0.7781.' },
  'Solve for x: log base 2 (x - 1) = 3.': { t: 'Indices and logarithms', e: 'The equation means x - 1 = 2^3 = 8, so x = 9.' },
  'Simplify: sqrt(75).': { t: 'Number operations', e: '75 = 25 x 3, so sqrt(75) = 5sqrt(3).' },
  'Simplify: sqrt(32).': { t: 'Number operations', e: '32 = 16 x 2, so sqrt(32) = 4sqrt(2).' },
  'Simplify: 3sqrt(2) x 2sqrt(3).': { t: 'Number operations', e: 'Multiply the numbers and the roots: 3 x 2 = 6 and sqrt(2) x sqrt(3) = sqrt(6), giving 6sqrt(6).' },
  'Express sqrt(50) + sqrt(18) in the form a sqrt(b).': { t: 'Number operations', e: 'sqrt(50) = 5sqrt(2) and sqrt(18) = 3sqrt(2), so the sum is 8sqrt(2).' },
  'Rationalise the denominator: 3/sqrt(7).': { t: 'Number operations', e: 'Multiply top and bottom by sqrt(7): 3sqrt(7)/7.' },
  'Simplify: sqrt(27) - sqrt(12).': { t: 'Number operations', e: 'sqrt(27) = 3sqrt(3) and sqrt(12) = 2sqrt(3), so the difference is sqrt(3).' },
  'If A = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5} and B = {2, 4, 6, 8}, find A intersect B.': { t: 'Sets and Venn diagrams', e: 'The intersection lists only the elements found in both sets: {2, 4}.' },
  'If P = {a, b, c, d} and Q = {c, d, e}, find P union Q.': { t: 'Sets and Venn diagrams', e: 'The union combines every element without repetition: {a, b, c, d, e}.' },
  'A set has 8 elements. How many subsets does it have?': { t: 'Sets and Venn diagrams', e: 'A set with n elements has 2^n subsets, so 2^8 = 256.' },
  'In a class of 50 students, 30 play football, 25 play tennis and every student plays at least one game. How many play both games?': { t: 'Sets and Venn diagrams', e: 'Since every student plays at least one game, both games = 30 + 25 - 50 = 5.' },
  'If n(A) = 12, n(B) = 9 and n(A union B) = 15, find n(A intersect B).': { t: 'Sets and Venn diagrams', e: 'n(A intersect B) = n(A) + n(B) - n(A union B) = 12 + 9 - 15 = 6.' },
  'In a group of 40 people, 25 speak English, 20 speak French and 8 speak both languages. How many speak neither language?': { t: 'Sets and Venn diagrams', e: 'Speaking at least one language = 25 + 20 - 8 = 37, so 40 - 37 = 3 speak neither.' },

  /* --- 2026-10-11: bank expansion — Algebraic Processes --- */
  'Simplify: 5x - 2y - 3x + 4y.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Collect like terms: 5x - 3x = 2x and -2y + 4y = 2y, giving 2x + 2y.' },
  'Expand and simplify: 2(x - 3) - 3(x - 1).': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Expand: 2x - 6 - 3x + 3 = -x - 3.' },
  'Factorise: x^2 + 5x.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'The common factor is x: x^2 + 5x = x(x + 5).' },
  'Simplify: (3x^2 - 5x + 2) - (x^2 - 4x + 7).': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Remove the bracket carefully: 3x^2 - 5x + 2 - x^2 + 4x - 7 = 2x^2 - x - 5.' },
  'Make y the subject of the formula: x = 2y + 5.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Subtract 5 from both sides and divide by 2: y = (x - 5)/2.' },
  'If p(x) = x^2 - 3x + 2, find p(4).': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Substitute x = 4: 16 - 12 + 2 = 6.' },
  'Solve the equation: x^2 - 4x + 3 = 0.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Factorise: (x - 1)(x - 3) = 0, so x = 1 or x = 3.' },
  'Find the roots of the equation x^2 + 7x + 12 = 0.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Factorise: (x + 3)(x + 4) = 0, so the roots are -3 and -4.' },
  'The sum of the roots of the equation x^2 - 6x + 8 = 0 is:': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Sum of roots = -b/a = -(-6)/1 = 6.' },
  'The product of the roots of the equation x^2 + 5x - 14 = 0 is:': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Product of roots = c/a = -14/1 = -14.' },
  'One root of the equation x^2 - 9x + 20 = 0 is 4. Find the other root.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Product of roots = 20, so the other root is 20/4 = 5.' },
  'For what positive value of k does the equation x^2 + kx + 9 = 0 have equal roots?': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Equal roots mean the discriminant is zero: k^2 - 4 x 9 = 0, so k^2 = 36 and k = 6 (the positive value).' },
  'Solve the simultaneous equations 2x + y = 7 and x - y = 2.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Add the equations: 3x = 9, so x = 3; then y = 7 - 6 = 1.' },
  'Solve the simultaneous equations 3x + 2y = 12 and x = 2. Find y.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Substitute x = 2: 6 + 2y = 12, so 2y = 6 and y = 3.' },
  'Solve the simultaneous equations x + 2y = 8 and 2x + y = 7.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Double the first equation: 2x + 4y = 16. Subtract the second: 3y = 9, so y = 3 and x = 2.' },
  'A father is 3 times as old as his son. In 12 years he will be twice as old. How old is the son now?': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Let the son be s years; the father is 3s. Then 3s + 12 = 2(s + 12), which gives s = 12.' },
  'Solve the simultaneous equations 4x - 3y = 6 and 2x + 3y = 12.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Add the equations: 6x = 18, so x = 3; then 3y = 12 - 6 = 6, so y = 2.' },
  'Solve the simultaneous equations y = x + 1 and y = 2x - 1.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Set the two expressions for y equal: x + 1 = 2x - 1, so x = 2 and y = 3.' },
  'y varies directly as x. If y = 15 when x = 5, find the constant of variation.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'y = kx; 15 = 5k, so k = 3.' },
  'y varies inversely as x. If y = 4 when x = 6, find y when x = 8.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'xy = k = 24; when x = 8, y = 24/8 = 3.' },
  'y varies directly as the square of x. If y = 36 when x = 3, find y when x = 5.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'y = kx^2; 36 = 9k, so k = 4. When x = 5, y = 4 x 25 = 100.' },
  'z varies jointly as x and y. If z = 12 when x = 2 and y = 3, find z when x = 4 and y = 5.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'z = kxy; 12 = 6k, so k = 2. When x = 4 and y = 5, z = 2 x 4 x 5 = 40.' },
  'y varies inversely as the square root of x. If y = 6 when x = 4, find y when x = 9.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'y = k/sqrt(x); 6 = k/2, so k = 12. When x = 9, y = 12/3 = 4.' },
  'The cost of making a chair varies directly as the number of chairs made. If 5 chairs cost N7,500, find the cost of 8 chairs.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Cost per chair = 7,500/5 = N1,500, so 8 chairs cost 8 x 1,500 = N12,000.' },
  'Solve the inequality: 2x - 3 > 7.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Add 3 to both sides: 2x > 10, so x > 5.' },
  'Solve the inequality: 3x + 2 <= 11.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Subtract 2: 3x <= 9, so x <= 3.' },
  'Solve the inequality: -2x < 6.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Divide both sides by -2 and reverse the sign: x > -3.' },
  'Solve the inequality: 5 - x >= 2.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Rearrange: -x >= -3, so x <= 3 (the sign flips when multiplying by -1).' },
  'Solve the inequality: x^2 <= 9.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'x^2 <= 9 means x lies between -3 and 3: -3 <= x <= 3.' },
  'Solve the inequality: 4 - 3x < 10.': { t: 'Algebra', e: 'Subtract 4: -3x < 6; divide by -3 and flip the sign: x > -2.' },
  'If A has first row 1, 2 and second row 3, 4, and B has first row 0, 1 and second row 2, 3, find A + B.': { t: 'Vectors and matrices', e: 'Add matching entries: first row 1 + 0, 2 + 1 and second row 3 + 2, 4 + 3, giving first row 1, 3 and second row 5, 7.' },
  'Find the determinant of the 2 x 2 matrix with first row 5, 2 and second row 3, 1.': { t: 'Vectors and matrices', e: 'Determinant = (5 x 1) - (2 x 3) = 5 - 6 = -1.' },
  'A matrix has first row 1, 0 and second row 0, 1. This matrix is:': { t: 'Vectors and matrices', e: 'Multiplying by this matrix leaves any matrix unchanged, so it is the identity matrix.' },
  'For what value of x is the matrix with first row x, 3 and second row 2, 4 singular?': { t: 'Vectors and matrices', e: 'Singular means determinant zero: 4x - 6 = 0, so x = 1.5.' },
  'If A has first row 2, 0 and second row 0, 5, find A squared (A x A).': { t: 'Vectors and matrices', e: 'Multiply out: first row 2 x 2, 0 and second row 0, 5 x 5, giving first row 4, 0 and second row 0, 25.' },
  'The transpose of the matrix with first row 1, 2 and second row 3, 4 is the matrix with:': { t: 'Vectors and matrices', e: 'The transpose swaps rows with columns, giving first row 1, 3 and second row 2, 4.' },
  'Find the 8th term of the arithmetic progression 5, 8, 11, ...': { t: 'Sequences and series', e: 'a = 5 and d = 3, so the 8th term = 5 + 7 x 3 = 26.' },
  'The first term of an arithmetic progression is 7 and the 10th term is 34. Find the common difference.': { t: 'Sequences and series', e: '34 = 7 + 9d, so 9d = 27 and d = 3.' },
  'Find the sum of the first 20 terms of the arithmetic progression with first term 1 and common difference 3.': { t: 'Sequences and series', e: 'S20 = 20/2 x (2 x 1 + 19 x 3) = 10 x 59 = 590.' },
  'Find the 5th term of the geometric progression 3, 6, 12, ...': { t: 'Sequences and series', e: 'a = 3 and r = 2, so the 5th term = 3 x 2^4 = 48.' },
  'Find the sum to infinity of the geometric progression 9, 3, 1, ...': { t: 'Sequences and series', e: 'a = 9 and r = 1/3, so the sum to infinity = a/(1 - r) = 9/(2/3) = 13.5.' },
  'The 3rd term of a geometric progression is 12 and the common ratio is 2. Find the first term.': { t: 'Sequences and series', e: 'ar^2 = 12 and r = 2, so 4a = 12 and a = 3.' },

  /* --- 2026-10-11: bank expansion — Mensuration & Plane Geometry --- */
  'Find the perimeter of a square of side 9 cm.': { t: 'Mensuration', e: 'Perimeter of a square = 4 x side = 4 x 9 = 36 cm.' },
  'Find the area of a square whose perimeter is 36 cm.': { t: 'Mensuration', e: 'Side = 36/4 = 9 cm, so the area = 9 x 9 = 81 cm^2.' },
  'Find the area of a rectangle of length 15 cm and breadth 8 cm.': { t: 'Mensuration', e: 'Area = length x breadth = 15 x 8 = 120 cm^2.' },
  'The area of a triangle is 30 cm^2 and its base is 12 cm. Find its height.': { t: 'Mensuration', e: 'Area = 1/2 x base x height, so 30 = 1/2 x 12 x h, giving h = 5 cm.' },
  'A rectangular room is 6 m long and 4 m wide. Find the cost of tiling its floor at N500 per square metre.': { t: 'Mensuration', e: 'Floor area = 6 x 4 = 24 m^2, so the cost = 24 x 500 = N12,000.' },
  'Find the perimeter of the sector of a circle of radius 7 cm and angle 90 degrees. Take pi = 22/7.': { t: 'Mensuration', e: 'Arc length = 90/360 x 2 x 22/7 x 7 = 11 cm, so the perimeter = 7 + 7 + 11 = 25 cm.' },
  'Find the total surface area of a cube of side 4 cm.': { t: 'Mensuration', e: 'A cube has 6 equal faces: total surface area = 6 x 4^2 = 96 cm^2.' },
  'Find the volume of a cylinder of radius 7 cm and height 10 cm. Take pi = 22/7.': { t: 'Mensuration', e: 'V = pi r^2 h = 22/7 x 49 x 10 = 1,540 cm^3.' },
  'Find the total surface area of a cuboid of dimensions 10 cm by 8 cm by 6 cm.': { t: 'Mensuration', e: 'Total surface area = 2(lw + lh + wh) = 2(80 + 60 + 48) = 376 cm^2.' },
  'A cylindrical tank has radius 1.4 m and height 5 m. Find its capacity in cubic metres. Take pi = 22/7.': { t: 'Mensuration', e: 'V = pi r^2 h = 22/7 x 1.96 x 5 = 30.8 m^3.' },
  'Find the volume of a cone of radius 3 cm and height 7 cm. Take pi = 22/7.': { t: 'Mensuration', e: 'V = 1/3 x pi x r^2 x h = 1/3 x 22/7 x 9 x 7 = 66 cm^3.' },
  'Find the total surface area of a hemisphere of radius 7 cm. Take pi = 22/7.': { t: 'Mensuration', e: 'Curved part = 2 x 22/7 x 49 = 308 cm^2; flat circular face = 22/7 x 49 = 154 cm^2; total = 462 cm^2.' },
  'Two angles are complementary. If one is 35 degrees, find the other.': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'Complementary angles add to 90 degrees: 90 - 35 = 55.' },
  'Find each exterior angle of a regular pentagon.': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'Each exterior angle = 360/5 = 72 degrees.' },
  'Find each interior angle of a regular octagon.': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'Sum of interior angles = (8 - 2) x 180 = 1080 degrees, so each angle = 1080/8 = 135 degrees.' },
  'The angles of a triangle are x, 2x and 3x degrees. Find x.': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'x + 2x + 3x = 180, so 6x = 180 and x = 30.' },
  'A right-angled triangle has one angle of 40 degrees. Find the other acute angle.': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'The acute angles of a right-angled triangle add to 90 degrees: 90 - 40 = 50.' },
  'An isosceles triangle has one angle of 100 degrees. Find each of the equal angles.': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'The equal angles add to 180 - 100 = 80, so each is 80/2 = 40 degrees.' },
  'Find the diameter of a circle of area 154 cm^2. Take pi = 22/7.': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'pi r^2 = 154, so r^2 = 49 and r = 7 cm; the diameter is 2 x 7 = 14 cm.' },
  'The opposite angles of a cyclic quadrilateral are in the ratio 2 : 3. Find the smaller angle.': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'Opposite angles of a cyclic quadrilateral add to 180 degrees: 2x + 3x = 180, so x = 36 and the smaller angle is 72.' },
  'A chord of length 24 cm is 5 cm from the centre of a circle. Find the radius of the circle.': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'The half-chord is 12 cm, so r^2 = 12^2 + 5^2 = 169 and r = 13 cm.' },
  'Two tangents from an external point touch a circle at points P and Q. The angle between the tangents is 70 degrees. Find the angle POQ at the centre.': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'The radii to P and Q are perpendicular to the tangents: 90 + 90 + 70 + angle POQ = 360, so angle POQ = 110 degrees.' },
  'Angles in the same segment of a circle are:': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'Angles standing on the same arc (in the same segment) are equal.' },
  'Find the area of a semicircle of radius 7 cm. Take pi = 22/7.': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'Area of the full circle = 22/7 x 49 = 154 cm^2, so the semicircle is 154/2 = 77 cm^2.' },
  'The point equidistant from the three vertices of a triangle is the:': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'The circumcentre is where the perpendicular bisectors of the sides meet, and it is equidistant from the three vertices.' },
  'The point equidistant from the three sides of a triangle is the:': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'The incentre is where the angle bisectors meet, and it is equidistant from the three sides.' },
  'To bisect a given line segment, you construct its:': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'Bisecting a segment means constructing its perpendicular bisector.' },
  'A point P moves so that OP <= 5 cm, where O is a fixed point. The locus of P is:': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'Every position of P lies no further than 5 cm from O, so the locus is the region inside and on the circle of radius 5 cm.' },
  'Which instrument is used to draw accurate circles and arcs in geometric constructions?': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'A pair of compasses draws circles and arcs of a chosen radius.' },
  'A goat is tethered to a stake with a 4 m rope. The shape of the region it can graze is:': { t: 'Geometry', e: 'Every reachable point is at most 4 m from the stake, so the grazing region is a circle of radius 4 m.' },

  /* --- 2026-10-11: bank expansion — Coordinate Geometry & Trigonometry --- */
  'Find the gradient of the line joining the points (-2, 3) and (4, 15).': { t: 'Coordinate geometry', e: 'Gradient = (15 - 3)/(4 - (-2)) = 12/6 = 2.' },
  'Find the y-intercept of the line 3x + 4y = 12.': { t: 'Coordinate geometry', e: 'On the y-axis, x = 0: 4y = 12, so y = 3.' },
  'Find the equation of the line passing through (2, 3) with gradient 2.': { t: 'Coordinate geometry', e: 'y = 2x + c; substituting (2, 3): 3 = 4 + c, so c = -1 and y = 2x - 1.' },
  'The lines y = 3x + 2 and y = 3x - 5 are:': { t: 'Coordinate geometry', e: 'Both lines have gradient 3 but different intercepts, so they never meet: they are parallel.' },
  'Find the midpoint of the points (-4, 7) and (6, -3).': { t: 'Coordinate geometry', e: 'Midpoint = ((-4 + 6)/2, (7 + (-3))/2) = (1, 2).' },
  'A line has gradient -1 and passes through (3, 2). Find its equation.': { t: 'Coordinate geometry', e: 'y = -x + c; substituting (3, 2): 2 = -3 + c, so c = 5 and y = -x + 5.' },
  'Find the gradient of the curve y = x^2 at the point where x = 3.': { t: 'Coordinate geometry', e: 'dy/dx = 2x, so at x = 3 the gradient is 6.' },
  'Find the equation of the circle with centre (2, -1) and radius 3.': { t: 'Coordinate geometry', e: 'Use (x - a)^2 + (y - b)^2 = r^2 with centre (2, -1) and radius 3: (x - 2)^2 + (y + 1)^2 = 9.' },
  'The centre of the circle x^2 + y^2 + 6x - 4y + 4 = 0 is:': { t: 'Coordinate geometry', e: 'Complete the square: x^2 + 6x = (x + 3)^2 - 9 and y^2 - 4y = (y - 2)^2 - 4, so the centre is (-3, 2).' },
  'Find the coordinates of the points where the line y = x + 1 meets the curve y = x^2 - 1.': { t: 'Coordinate geometry', e: 'Set x + 1 = x^2 - 1: x^2 - x - 2 = 0, so (x - 2)(x + 1) = 0. The points are (2, 3) and (-1, 0).' },
  'The line y = 2x + 3 intersects the y-axis at:': { t: 'Coordinate geometry', e: 'On the y-axis, x = 0, so y = 3: the point is (0, 3).' },
  'A curve has equation y = x^2 - 2x - 3. Find the values of x where it crosses the x-axis.': { t: 'Coordinate geometry', e: 'Set y = 0 and factorise: x^2 - 2x - 3 = (x - 3)(x + 1) = 0, so x = -1 or x = 3.' },
  'Evaluate: tan 30 degrees.': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'tan 30 degrees = 1/sqrt(3).' },
  'Simplify: tan theta x cos theta.': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'tan theta = sin theta / cos theta, so tan theta x cos theta = sin theta.' },
  'Express cos 240 degrees as a trigonometric ratio of an acute angle.': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'cos 240 = cos(180 + 60) = -cos 60 degrees.' },
  'If cos theta = 12/13 and theta is acute, find sin theta.': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'sin^2 theta + cos^2 theta = 1, so sin theta = sqrt(1 - (12/13)^2) = 5/13.' },
  'In triangle ABC, angle C = 90 degrees, AC = 9 cm and BC = 12 cm. Find sin A.': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'AB = sqrt(9^2 + 12^2) = 15 cm; sin A = opposite/hypotenuse = 12/15 = 4/5.' },
  'Solve for theta in the range 0 degrees to 90 degrees: cos theta = sqrt(3)/2.': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'cos 30 degrees = sqrt(3)/2, so theta = 30 degrees.' },
  'A ladder 15 m long leans against a wall making an angle of 30 degrees with the ground. How high up the wall does it reach?': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'Height = length x sin(angle with the ground) = 15 x sin 30 = 15 x 0.5 = 7.5 m.' },
  'From the top of a cliff 80 m high, the angle of depression of a boat at sea is 45 degrees. How far is the boat from the foot of the cliff?': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'With a 45-degree angle of depression the height equals the horizontal distance, so the boat is 80 m away.' },
  'A plane flies 100 km due east from P to Q, then 100 km due south from Q to R. Find the bearing of R from P.': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'The route turns a right angle at Q and the two legs are equal, so R lies south-east of P: bearing 135 degrees.' },
  'The bearing of X from Y is 195 degrees. Find the bearing of Y from X.': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'A back bearing differs by 180 degrees: 195 - 180 = 015 degrees.' },
  'A tower is 30 m tall. The angle of elevation of its top from a point on the ground is 60 degrees. How far is the point from the foot of the tower?': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'tan 60 = height/distance, so distance = 30/tan 60 = 30/sqrt(3) = 10sqrt(3) m.' },
  'Town B is 60 km east of town A. Town C is 80 km south of B. Find the distance from A to C.': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'The path A to B to C forms a right-angled triangle at B: AC = sqrt(60^2 + 80^2) = 100 km.' },
  'The graph of y = cos x crosses the x-axis first at:': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'cos x first becomes 0 at x = 90 degrees.' },
  'The period of the graph of y = cos 3x is:': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'Period = 360 divided by the coefficient of x = 360/3 = 120 degrees.' },
  'The minimum value of y = 2 sin x is:': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'sin x ranges from -1 to 1, so 2 sin x ranges from -2 to 2; the minimum is -2.' },
  'The graph of y = sin x has its maximum value at x =': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'y = sin x peaks at 1 when x = 90 degrees.' },
  'For 0 degrees <= x <= 360 degrees, how many solutions does the equation tan x = 1 have?': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'tan x = 1 at 45 degrees and again at 225 degrees, giving 2 solutions.' },
  'The amplitude of y = 4 sin 2x is:': { t: 'Trigonometry', e: 'The amplitude is the coefficient of the sine term: 4.' },

  /* --- 2026-10-11: bank expansion — Calculus, Statistics & Vectors --- */
  'Differentiate: y = 4x^3 - 2x + 5.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'Differentiate term by term: 4x^3 gives 12x^2, -2x gives -2, and the constant 5 gives 0. So dy/dx = 12x^2 - 2.' },
  'Differentiate: y = x^2 + 3/x.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'Write 3/x as 3x^-1, so dy/dx = 2x - 3x^-2 = 2x - 3/x^2.' },
  'If y = 5 sin x, find dy/dx.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'The derivative of sin x is cos x, so dy/dx = 5 cos x.' },
  'Differentiate: y = (3x - 1)^5.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'Chain rule: dy/dx = 5(3x - 1)^4 x 3 = 15(3x - 1)^4.' },
  'Find the gradient of the curve y = x^3 - 2x at the point where x = 2.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'dy/dx = 3x^2 - 2; at x = 2 this is 12 - 2 = 10.' },
  'If y = 7, find dy/dx.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'y = 7 is a constant, and the gradient of a constant is 0.' },
  'Integrate 4x^3 with respect to x.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'Add 1 to the power and divide by the new power: 4x^4/4 = x^4 + C.' },
  'Evaluate: integral from 0 to 3 of 2x dx.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'The integral is x^2, so the value is 9 - 0 = 9.' },
  'Integrate (3x^2 + 4x - 5) with respect to x.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'Integrate term by term: x^3 + 2x^2 - 5x + C.' },
  'Evaluate: integral from 2 to 4 of 3 dx.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'The integral of the constant 3 is 3x, so the value is 12 - 6 = 6.' },
  'Integrate 2 sin x with respect to x.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'The integral of sin x is -cos x, so the answer is -2 cos x + C.' },
  'Evaluate: integral from 0 to 2 of (x^2 + 1) dx.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'The integral is x^3/3 + x, so the value is 8/3 + 2 = 14/3.' },
  'Find the gradient of the tangent to the curve y = x^2 - 3x at the point where x = 1.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'dy/dx = 2x - 3; at x = 1 the gradient is 2 - 3 = -1.' },
  'The velocity v m/s of a particle is v = 3t^2 + 2. Find its acceleration when t = 1.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'Acceleration = dv/dt = 6t; at t = 1 it is 6 m/s^2.' },
  'Find the area under the curve y = 2x from x = 1 to x = 3.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'The integral of 2x is x^2, so the area = 9 - 1 = 8.' },
  'Find the coordinates of the minimum point of the curve y = x^2 + 4x + 5.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'dy/dx = 2x + 4 = 0 at x = -2; then y = 4 - 8 + 5 = 1, so the minimum is (-2, 1).' },
  'A particle moves with velocity v = 2t + 3 m/s. Find the distance travelled in the first 4 seconds.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'Distance = integral of (2t + 3) from 0 to 4 = t^2 + 3t, giving 16 + 12 = 28 m.' },
  'The side of a cube increases at 2 cm/s. Find the rate of increase of its volume when the side is 5 cm.': { t: 'Calculus', e: 'V = s^3, so dV/dt = 3s^2 x ds/dt = 3 x 25 x 2 = 75 cm^3/s.' },
  'A pie chart has a sector angle of 72 degrees representing 36 students. How many students does the whole chart represent?': { t: 'Statistics', e: '72 degrees represents 36 students, so 1 degree represents 0.5 students; the full 360 degrees represents 180 students.' },
  'The class intervals of a distribution are 1-10, 11-20, 21-30. The class boundaries of the class 11-20 are:': { t: 'Statistics', e: 'The gap between classes is shared, so the class 11-20 runs from 10.5 up to 20.5.' },
  'In a frequency table, the class width of the class 15-24 is:': { t: 'Statistics', e: 'Class width = upper boundary - lower boundary = 24.5 - 14.5 = 10.' },
  'The scores of a test are grouped 0-9, 10-19, 20-29. The class mark of the class 10-19 is:': { t: 'Statistics', e: 'Class mark = midpoint = (10 + 19)/2 = 14.5.' },
  'A frequency polygon is drawn by joining:': { t: 'Statistics', e: 'A frequency polygon joins the midpoints of the tops of consecutive bars.' },
  'In a distribution the frequency of the first, second and third classes are 4, 7 and 5. What is the cumulative frequency of the fourth class if its frequency is 6?': { t: 'Statistics', e: 'Cumulative frequency keeps a running total: 4 + 7 + 5 + 6 = 22.' },
  'Find the mean of 6, 7, 8, 9 and 10.': { t: 'Statistics', e: 'Sum = 40, so the mean = 40/5 = 8.' },
  'Find the median of 12, 15, 11, 18 and 14.': { t: 'Statistics', e: 'Arrange in order: 11, 12, 14, 15, 18. The middle value is 14.' },
  'The mean of four numbers is 9. Three of them are 8, 10 and 12. Find the fourth number.': { t: 'Statistics', e: 'The total is 4 x 9 = 36; the three known numbers add to 30, so the fourth is 6.' },
  'Find the median of 3, 8, 5, 9, 12 and 7.': { t: 'Statistics', e: 'Arrange in order: 3, 5, 7, 8, 9, 12. The median is the mean of the middle pair: (7 + 8)/2 = 7.5.' },
  'Find the range of the numbers 23, 17, 35, 29 and 12.': { t: 'Statistics', e: 'Range = highest - lowest = 35 - 12 = 23.' },
  'A distribution has no mode when:': { t: 'Statistics', e: 'There is no mode when every value occurs equally often, so no value stands out.' },
  'A number is chosen at random from 1 to 20. Find the probability that it is a multiple of 5.': { t: 'Probability', e: 'The multiples of 5 from 1 to 20 are 5, 10, 15 and 20: 4 out of 20 = 1/5.' },
  'A fair die is thrown once. Find the probability of getting a number greater than 4.': { t: 'Probability', e: 'Only 5 and 6 qualify: 2 out of 6 = 1/3.' },
  'A bag contains 6 white and 4 black balls. One ball is drawn at random. Find the probability that it is black.': { t: 'Probability', e: 'P(black) = 4/(6 + 4) = 4/10 = 2/5.' },
  'Two dice are thrown together. Find the probability that the sum is 7.': { t: 'Probability', e: 'The pairs adding to 7 are (1,6), (2,5), (3,4), (4,3), (5,2), (6,1): 6 out of 36 = 1/6.' },
  'The probability that it rains on a given day is 0.25. Find the probability that it does not rain.': { t: 'Probability', e: 'P(no rain) = 1 - 0.25 = 0.75.' },
  'A card is drawn from a standard pack of 52 cards. Find the probability that it is a spade or a heart.': { t: 'Probability', e: 'Spades and hearts make up half the pack: 26/52 = 1/2.' },
  'Evaluate: 5!.': { t: 'Permutations and combinations', e: '5! = 5 x 4 x 3 x 2 x 1 = 120.' },
  'In how many ways can 4 students be selected from 9 students?': { t: 'Permutations and combinations', e: 'Order does not matter, so it is 9C4 = 9!/(4! x 5!) = 126.' },
  'How many ways can the letters of the word NUMBER be arranged?': { t: 'Permutations and combinations', e: 'NUMBER has 6 different letters, so the arrangements = 6! = 720.' },
  'In how many ways can a committee of 2 boys and 2 girls be chosen from 5 boys and 4 girls?': { t: 'Permutations and combinations', e: 'Choose the boys and girls separately: 5C2 x 4C2 = 10 x 6 = 60 ways.' },
  'How many 4-digit numbers can be formed from the digits 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6 if no digit is repeated?': { t: 'Permutations and combinations', e: 'The digits fill the places one at a time: 6 x 5 x 4 x 3 = 360.' },
  'Evaluate: 7P2.': { t: 'Permutations and combinations', e: '7P2 = 7 x 6 = 42.' },
  'If a = (3, 4), find the vector 2a.': { t: 'Vectors and matrices', e: 'Multiply each component by 2: (6, 8).' },
  'Find the magnitude of the vector (5, 12).': { t: 'Vectors and matrices', e: 'Magnitude = sqrt(5^2 + 12^2) = sqrt(169) = 13.' },
  'Given a = (1, 2) and b = (3, 1), find 2a + b.': { t: 'Vectors and matrices', e: '2a = (2, 4); adding b = (3, 1) gives (5, 5).' },
  'The vectors (2, 4) and (k, 8) are parallel. Find k.': { t: 'Vectors and matrices', e: 'Parallel vectors keep the same ratio between components: 2/4 = k/8, so k = 4.' },
  'If a = (2, 5), find -a.': { t: 'Vectors and matrices', e: 'The negative vector reverses both components: (-2, -5).' },
  'A vector with magnitude 1 is called a:': { t: 'Vectors and matrices', e: 'A unit vector has magnitude 1.' },
  'The image of the point (4, 7) under the translation by vector (3, -2) is:': { t: 'Vectors and matrices', e: 'Add the vector: (4 + 3, 7 - 2) = (7, 5).' },
  'The reflection of the point (-6, 2) in the y-axis is:': { t: 'Vectors and matrices', e: 'Reflection in the y-axis flips the sign of x: (-6, 2) becomes (6, 2).' },
  'A square of side 3 cm is enlarged by scale factor 3. Find the perimeter of the image.': { t: 'Vectors and matrices', e: 'Scale factor 3 makes the side 9 cm, so the perimeter = 4 x 9 = 36 cm.' },
  'The matrix with first row -1, 0 and second row 0, 1 represents a reflection in the:': { t: 'Vectors and matrices', e: 'The matrix sends x to -x and keeps y unchanged, which is a reflection in the y-axis.' },
  'The image of the point (3, -2) under a rotation of 90 degrees clockwise about the origin is:': { t: 'Vectors and matrices', e: 'A 90-degree clockwise turn sends (x, y) to (y, -x): (3, -2) becomes (-2, -3).' },
  'Which transformation changes only the position of a shape, with every point moving the same distance in the same direction?': { t: 'Vectors and matrices', e: 'Only a translation slides every point the same distance in the same direction.' }
};
